      "writtenOn": "2017-10-25T14:11:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we deleting the logical port on a disable? Shouldn\u0027t this only be done on a delete of the ONU?",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_170600cf",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-26T06:21:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we disable and enable the ports, the ONOS is not pushing the flows but when we delete and then add the ports the ONOS sends the flows again.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_cc0fbfe0",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_d799886f",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-26T15:20:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Deleting and re-creating the port is a bit too destructive for a simple disable/enable, and also we generate a new port number in ONOS every time we do this. \nMy suggestion would be to store whatever data from the flow rules that the adapter needs (which is just the CVID I believe) and then re-send the relevant OMCI when the ONU becomes active again.\nAlso, if there is an issue in ONOS and we believe that flow rules should get pushed down on a port enable/disable, then we should raise a bug for that instead of trying to work around the issue in the adapter.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_170600cf",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_97db10ed",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-26T18:05:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Peter,\nWhen you say generation of port number from ONOS, are you talking about logical port number?\nAgree that if ONOS is not sending flow while disable/enable, we need to rise a bug and track it. For now my suggestion is to take this changes as workaround and not to store any information in adapter because it may affect HA cases.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_d799886f",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_975e7044",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-26T18:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Raghu,\nI am ok with this implementation as a work-around but I think we are in agreement that this is not architecturally correct. If you could please raise a bug to track this and reference it here I will approve these changes.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_97db10ed",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_f71dac74",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000129
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-26T19:07:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually as I was typing this comment we had started a conversation with David Bainbridge regarding how ONOS should handle the enable/disable case. He had advised against deleting the port and is suggesting to change the logical port state instead (OFPPS_BLOCKED/OFPPS_LIVE) and have that trigger the flow rule re-addition. If you could raise the bug and perhaps allow David till tomorrow to look at this it may be a simple change in ONOS...in which case we can implement this the correct way with no workarounds...thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_975e7044",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_524ec6c2",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-27T05:03:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Peter,\ni just cross checked implementation of disable/enable in other onu adapters(as in adtran_onu.py) wherein i see delete logical port during disable(self.adapter_agent.delete_logical_port(logical_device_id, port)).\n\nLet me know if you want me to break away from this as i had tried using OFPPS_DOWN/OFPPS_LIVE which could not solve this issue. I would not term this as a workaround as its been implemented in other onu adapters also.\nIf we still have a agreement that we must move towards a different approach we can create a JIRA user story and work on it and allow this change to be merged as part of the current user story.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_f71dac74",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5c5d37_72ad4a31",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/broadcom_onu/broadcom_onu.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 338,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000003
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-27T15:02:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not ok with this as a work around. Completely agree that we need to file a bug with ONOS if we expect flows to be re-pushed on enable, but deleting and re-adding is not a proper work around. If we need a work around I would follow what Peter suggested about saving the required information on disable and then using that information on enable. \n\nI will check into the ONOS issue. Need to check the standard to understand if controllers are meant to re-push on enable. It may be that the save the state is the best solution depending on the standard. Saving the state may be what an OF switch is meant to do.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_97db10ed",
      "revId": "3488e7e16f951a50f0213f8f8decdbaffbb69c36",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
